<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cynoscephalae (364 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">364 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cynoscephalae in 364 BCE was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> between a Theban-led army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelopidas">Pelopidas</a> and Alexander, tyrant of Pherae. The Thebans and their Thessalian allies won the battle, but Pelopidas was killed while charging at Alexander in person. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> later forced Alexander to submit, but the loss of Pelopidas deprived the city of one of its two great commanders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cynoscephalae-364-bce.jpg" alt="Battle of Cynoscephalae (364 BCE)" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Megistias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:362BCThebanHegemony.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
